@page "/demo/pickers"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using Fx.ControlKit
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared

@* 2026-10-19: new page (Baaria approved the Control tour split; third page). The tour's Selection tab moved here and was removed
   there. Of that tab, RadioGroupControl already lives on Checks & switches and CalendarControl and TimePickerControl on Date & time,
   so this page carries AutoCompleteControl, StepperControl and ColorPaletteControl; DropDownListControl (29 parameters) is proposed
   as a page of its own (SC-279). Documentation written from AutoCompleteControl.razor, StepperControl.razor, WizardModels.cs,
   ColorPaletteControl.razor and ColorPalettes.cs; rows checked with scratchpad/vocabcheck.py; behaviour sentences read from
   SearchAsync/CommitAsync, CanSelect/SelectAsync/KeyAsync and SelectAsync/KeyAsync/OnParametersSet. *@

<PageTitle>Pickers &amp; selectors — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Pickers &amp; selectors" Category="Components" CategoryHref="components"
                   ControlName="AutoCompleteControl · StepperControl · ColorPaletteControl"
                   Tagline="Suggestions while typing, a step indicator that knows which steps may be entered, and a colour palette."
                   SourcePath="AutoCompleteControl.razor;StepperControl.razor;WizardModels.cs;ColorPaletteControl.razor;ColorPalettes.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            Three small controls that pick one thing. <code>AutoCompleteControl</code> is an editable dropdown whose popup fills with
            suggestions while the user types, from a list it filters itself or from a callback you supply; its value is the text, and it tells
            you separately when that text is one of the suggestions. <code>StepperControl</code> draws the steps of a process as buttons and
            decides which of them may be entered: in linear mode only earlier steps and the next one, never past an invalid step, never a
            disabled step. <code>ColorPaletteControl</code> is a grid of swatches with one focusable tile and arrow-key movement.
            Radio groups are on <a href="demo/checks">Checks &amp; switches</a>, calendars and time pickers on <a href="demo/date-time">Date &amp; time</a>.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="suggest" Title="Suggestions while typing" RazorCode="@Code.Suggest" CSharpCode="@Code.SuggestCs">
            <Description><p>Left: twelve cities filtered by the control, case-insensitive, anywhere in the name, after one character and a 250 ms pause; an <code>ItemTemplate</code> adds the country, and <code>ItemSelected</code> reports the city object once the text matches a suggestion. Right: <code>OnRead</code> answers from a callback that waits 300 ms like a server would, after two characters and a 400 ms pause, five suggestions at most; typing on cancels the previous lookup. In both, the bound value is the text, whether or not it came from the list.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="pair">
                    <div>
                        <p class="pane-title">From a list</p>
                        <AutoCompleteControl TItem="City" DataSource="@_cities" TextField="Name" @bind-Value="_cityText" ItemSelected="c => _pickedCity = c" Placeholder="Type a city" AriaLabel="City" Width="100%">
                            <ItemTemplate Context="city"><span>@city.Name</span> <span class="muted">@city.Country</span></ItemTemplate>
                        </AutoCompleteControl>
                        <p class="result">Text: @(_cityText ?? "") · Picked: @(_pickedCity is null ? "nothing yet" : $"{_pickedCity.Name}, {_pickedCity.Country}")</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <p class="pane-title">From a callback</p>
                        <AutoCompleteControl TItem="string" OnRead="LookupAsync" MinLength="2" DebounceDelay="400" MaxSuggestions="5" @bind-Value="_product" Placeholder="Type two letters" AriaLabel="Product" Width="100%" />
                        <p class="result">Text: @(_product ?? "") · @_lookups lookups so far.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="steps" Title="Steps" RazorCode="@Code.Steps" CSharpCode="@Code.StepsCs">
            <Description><p>Four steps in the default linear mode: any earlier step can be clicked, the next one too, the ones after it are disabled. Mark the current step invalid and it gains a warning sign while every later step closes, so Next does nothing until the step is valid again; going back is always allowed. The Back and Next buttons call <code>SelectAsync</code> from the page, <code>CanNavigate</code> sees every move before it happens, and the arrow keys walk from step to step.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="() => _stepper!.SelectAsync(_step - 1)" Disabled="@(_step == 0)">Back</ButtonControl>
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="() => _stepper!.SelectAsync(_step + 1)" Disabled="@(_step == _steps.Count - 1)">Next</ButtonControl>
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="() => _stepValid = !_stepValid">@(_stepValid ? "Mark this step invalid" : "Mark this step valid")</ButtonControl>
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <StepperControl @ref="_stepper" Steps="@_steps" @bind-Value="_step" InvalidSteps="@InvalidSteps" CanNavigate="Navigating" AriaLabel="Checkout steps" />
                <p class="result">Step @(_step + 1) of @_steps.Count: @_steps[_step].Title. @_navLog</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="palette" Title="Colour palette" RazorCode="@Code.Palette" CSharpCode="@Code.PaletteCs">
            <Description><p>Left: the built-in 48-colour palette, eight across. Right: ten colours of your own, five across, larger tiles, and a <code>TileTemplate</code> that prints the hex value instead of the tick. Click a swatch or move with the arrow keys, Home and End; Up and Down jump by a row. The selected swatch keeps an outline whatever the template shows.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="pair">
                    <div>
                        <p class="pane-title">Default palette</p>
                        <ColorPaletteControl @bind-Value="_color" />
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <p class="pane-title">Custom colours</p>
                        <ColorPaletteControl Colors="@_brand" Columns="5" TileSize="36px" @bind-Value="_accent" AriaLabel="Accent colour">
                            <TileTemplate Context="colour"><span class="tile-label">@colour.TrimStart('#')</span></TileTemplate>
                        </ColorPaletteControl>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="result"><span class="swatch" style="background:@_color"></span>@_color · <span class="swatch" style="background:@_accent"></span>@_accent</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-autocompletecontrol-titem-parameters" Title="AutoCompleteControl&lt;TItem&gt; parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Auto.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="AutoCompleteControl&lt;TItem&gt; parameters" Rows="Vocab.Auto" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-autocompletecontrol-events" Title="AutoCompleteControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.AutoEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="AutoCompleteControl events" Rows="Vocab.AutoEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-autocompletecontrol-methods" Title="AutoCompleteControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.AutoMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="AutoCompleteControl methods" Rows="Vocab.AutoMethods" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-autocompletecontrol-read-only-state" Title="AutoCompleteControl read-only state" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.AutoState.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="AutoCompleteControl read-only state" Rows="Vocab.AutoState" />
                <p>
                The text box and the popup are a <code>DropDownListControl</code> in editable mode. A search starts when the text has at least
                <code>MinLength</code> characters, waits <code>DebounceDelay</code> milliseconds, and is cancelled by the next keystroke. Without
                <code>OnRead</code> the suggestions are the items whose text contains the typed text, ignoring case. The popup opens when there is at
                least one suggestion and closes when there is none, when the text is too short, when the control is disabled, or when the page
                changes <code>Value</code>. An exception thrown by <code>OnRead</code> becomes <code>ErrorMessage</code>, shown under the box.
                </p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-steppercontrol-parameters" Title="StepperControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Stepper.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="StepperControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Stepper" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-steppercontrol-events" Title="StepperControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.StepperEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="StepperControl events" Rows="Vocab.StepperEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-steppercontrol-methods" Title="StepperControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.StepperMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="StepperControl methods" Rows="Vocab.StepperMethods" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-wizardstepdescriptor" Title="WizardStepDescriptor" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.StepDesc.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="WizardStepDescriptor" Rows="Vocab.StepDesc" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-wizardstepcontext-passed-to-steptemplate" Title="WizardStepContext, passed to StepTemplate" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.StepCtx.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="WizardStepContext, passed to StepTemplate" Rows="Vocab.StepCtx" />
                <p>
                A step can be entered when the control is enabled, no move is in progress, the step is not in <code>DisabledSteps</code>, and, in linear
                mode, it is at most one past the current step and the current step is not in <code>InvalidSteps</code> when moving forward. A step that
                cannot be entered renders as a disabled button. The current step carries <code>aria-current="step"</code>, an invalid step a warning
                sign, and each button's tooltip is the step's <code>Description</code>.
                </p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-colorpalettecontrol-parameters" Title="ColorPaletteControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Palette.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="ColorPaletteControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Palette" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-colorpalettecontrol-events" Title="ColorPaletteControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.PaletteEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="ColorPaletteControl events" Rows="Vocab.PaletteEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-colorpalettecontrol-methods" Title="ColorPaletteControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.PaletteMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="ColorPaletteControl methods" Rows="Vocab.PaletteMethods" />
                <p>
                Colours are compared ignoring case. <code>ColorPalettes.Basic</code> is the default list: 48 colours in six rows of eight. One swatch at a
                time is in the Tab order; it follows <code>Value</code> when the page changes it and the focus when the user moves with the keys.
                </p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-keyboard" Title="Keyboard" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Keys.Length, "keys")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Keyboard" Title="Keyboard" Rows="Vocab.Keys" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <p>
            The autocomplete box takes <code>AriaLabel</code>, sets <code>aria-busy</code> while it searches and announces "Loading suggestions…"
            through a status element. The stepper is a <code>nav</code> labelled by <code>AriaLabel</code>; its steps are buttons, the current one
            marked with <code>aria-current</code>, and steps that may not be entered are disabled rather than hidden. The palette is a
            <code>listbox</code> of <code>option</code> buttons, each labelled with its colour value and carrying <code>aria-selected</code>, with one
            tab stop and arrow-key movement.
        </p>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="demo/checks">Checks &amp; switches</a>: the radio group, for picking one of a few visible options.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/date-time">Date &amp; time</a>: calendar, date, time and time-span pickers.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/forms">Forms</a>: the dropdown editor a form item uses for enums and nullable booleans.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

